id: pm-z9x1r2
title: "Harness-aware author identity: pm resolves the acting agent from its runtime harness so PM_AUTHOR is never required"
description: ""
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",author,identity,provenance,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:45:04.396Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T02:36:59.831Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T02:36:59.000Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "A public SDK resolver detects the acting harness from environment and process ancestry, covering at minimum Claude Code, Codex, pi, opencode, Cursor, Aider, Gemini CLI, and generic CI, with an extension point for unknown harnesses; Resolution precedence is documented and tested: explicit --author, then PM_AUTHOR, then configured author_default, then harness detection, then anonymous; Every history entry records an author_source discriminator (asserted vs detected vs configured) so detected identity is never confused with verified identity; Detection is bounded and never blocks: a hard timeout and a pure-function fallback keep cold-start latency within the startup budget; Detected authors are recorded in a stable, greppable namespace (for example harness:claude-code) so downstream queries can filter by harness; Telemetry continues to receive only the hashed author context, with no raw harness-derived identity leaving the machine"
goal: agent-legible-surface
objective: An agent runs pm mutations with no identity ceremony and the recorded author is still accurate and provenanced
value: Every mutation an agent makes today must be prefixed with an environment variable that the agent has to be told about out of band; that prefix is pure token and instruction overhead repeated on every call.
impact: Removes the single most repeated piece of boilerplate in agent-facing pm usage and makes author attribution correct by default instead of correct by discipline.
outcome: "pm create/update/close invoked with no author configuration record a harness-derived author plus an author_source provenance field, and unknown-author events stop being produced by first-party agent runs."
why_now: "Author attribution enforcement shipped with a strict mode, but strict mode is unusable while correct attribution depends on every agent remembering an env var. Detection is the missing half."
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Implemented and merged harness-aware author resolution and immutable source provenance through the public SDK and CLI runtime.
expected_result: "Agent mutations require no PM_AUTHOR boilerplate while retaining deterministic, provenanced author identity."
actual_result: "All supported harnesses resolve through the shared primitive; create, update, and close produce no unknown author, with focused and packed-style temporary acceptance plus 6,291-test full coverage at 100/100/100/100."
