  "2026-07-25T02:02:06.258Z","harness:codex","Evidence: implemented public SDK runtime primitives for deterministic author resolution and harness detection (Codex, Claude Code, pi, OpenCode, Cursor, Aider, Gemini, CI), explicit/env/configured/harness precedence, provenance propagation through history, and portable source-workspace roots for sandboxed linked tests. Verified by the full 6,290-test coverage run at 100/100/100/100 and an anonymous packed-package consumer where PM_AUTHOR was unset and mutations recorded harness:codex."
  "2026-07-25T02:27:16.123Z",codex-root,"Regression evidence: on merged main 3a0c570c with PM_AUTHOR unset, pm close and pm update wrote author=unknown/author_source=unknown while comments, files, release, and other migrated paths wrote harness:codex. Health rose to 32 actionable unknown events. Scope is now every remaining direct PM_AUTHOR/default fallback in mutation-capable CLI/SDK paths, plus acknowledgements for the events generated during closeout."
  "2026-07-25T02:36:58.133Z","harness:codex","Post-merge remediation evidence: close.ts and update.ts now call the shared resolveAuthor primitive; focused test, typecheck, strict lint/static/docstring gates, and full coverage all pass. Full suite: 361 files, 6,291 tests, 100% statements 43,249/43,249, branches 30,704/30,704, functions 8,791/8,791, lines 42,030/42,030. Global installed acceptance recorded create as detected and later update/close as configured harness:codex after init persisted the detected default; the real repository update recorded detected harness:codex. All 32 bypass-generated closeout events were append-only acknowledged with evidence, restoring actionable_unknown_event_count=0 and health ok:true."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T02:02:06.885Z","harness:codex","Agent identity belongs in a deterministic SDK primitive: explicit, environment, configured, detected harness, then unknown. Harness detection must inspect bounded process metadata only and must never require a user-authored environment variable."
