close_reason: "Completed universal author parity after PR #693: update and close now use the shared harness resolver, regression coverage and full gates pass, and all bypass-generated events are acknowledged without history rewriting."
body: "## Problem\nCorrect authorship currently depends on every agent remembering to prefix mutations with PM_AUTHOR. That is out-of-band instruction cost on every call, it is silently skippable, and when skipped it produces unknown-author history events that the governance surface then has to triage.\n\n## Approach\nResolve identity from the runtime instead of from instruction. A harness detector inspects environment markers and process ancestry to name the acting agent, and the result is recorded alongside a provenance discriminator so that detected identity is never mistaken for cryptographically verified identity.\n\n## Boundary\nDetection is convenience, not authentication. Verifiable authorship is pm-u14c (per-entry signatures); authorization is pm-xc68 (principal policy). This item must not claim or imply verification, and strict-mode rejection semantics stay owned by the attribution enforcement work.\n\n## Prior art in this workspace\nErgonomic attribution (global --author, init author_default, unknown-author advisory) and attribution enforcement both shipped and closed; the telemetry agent-identity dimension already hashes PM_AUTHOR. This item adds the detection layer those three assumed would exist."
